/**
 * Renders nothing.
 *
 * Starlight's chrome is a tree of components that import each other, and its CSS ships because of the
 * *import*, not because anything renders. `Page.astro` imports `PageSidebar`, which imports
 * `MobileTableOfContents`, which imports `TableOfContentsList` — so three scoped stylesheets shipped on all 115
 * pages while zero pages carried any of their scope hashes. Pointing the top of such a subtree at this file
 * severs the import and the bytes go with it.
 *
 * Used for the components this site replaces outright, and for the ones it cannot reach a use for. Where a
 * Starlight feature is worth keeping, it gets a real Cornerstone override instead — see Banner.astro and
 * DraftContentNotice.astro, which keep working rather than silently doing nothing.
 */
---
